window.AG_CHAPTERS["15"] = {"id":"15","title":"The Fifth Watch","titleZh":"五更","patient":{"name":"Ferryman Wu 吳老渡","sprite":"man"},"scene":{"img":"art/scene-treatment.jpg","key":"rain"},"pattern":"Spleen and Kidney Yang Deficiency 脾腎陽虛","principle":"warm the yang of Spleen and Kidney, and let the water move by itself","tongue":"pale, swollen, tooth-marked, with a white slippery coating","pulseNote":{"en":"You must press to the bone to find it, and when you do it is slower than your own.","zh":"沉取始得，其至遲於己脈"},"needleAsk":{"en":"Needle <b>F&#249;li&#363; KI7</b>. Tap its exact location.","zh":"行針 — 點出穴位精確位置"},"target":{"id":"KI7","zh":"復溜","py":"F&#249;li&#363;","x":102,"y":780,"img":"art/body-leg-medial.jpg","w":434,"h":1159,"view":{"x":52,"y":696,"w":250,"h":368},"decoys":[{"x":113,"y":868},{"x":178,"y":722},{"x":78,"y":800},{"x":132,"y":892},{"x":146,"y":778}],"note":"<b>復溜 F&#249;li&#363; KI7</b> — two cun directly above T&#224;ix&#299; KI3, on the anterior border of the Achilles tendon. River point of the Kidney channel. It warms Kidney yang, moves water and reduces swelling, stops chronic diarrhoea, and secures the exterior against sweating.<br>太谿直上二寸，跟腱前緣。腎經經穴。溫腎陽、利水消腫、止久瀉、固表止汗。"},"hints":{"ask":{"en":"He told you the <b>hour</b> before he told you anything else. Ask about the hour.","zh":"其人先言時辰，而後及其餘。當問其時。"},"look":{"en":"A tongue that is pale, fat and wet is telling you about warmth, not about damp alone.","zh":"舌淡而胖且潤者，所言在陽，不獨在濕。"},"pulse":{"en":"Count it against your own breath. Depth and speed both matter here, and so does force.","zh":"以己息候之。此案沉浮、遲數、有力無力，三者皆須察。"},"dx":{"en":"Reason from the clock first, then from the chain, then from the water.","zh":"先從時辰推之，次從傳變推之，末從水推之。"},"rx":{"en":"Two organs are cold. Reach the lower one at its own channel, and the middle one where you always do.","zh":"二臟俱寒。下者取其本經，中者取其常穴。"},"tech":{"en":"He is empty and he is cold. There is nothing here to take away — only something to put back.","zh":"其人虛而且寒。無可奪者，惟有可與者。"}},"reactions":[{"who":"master","en":"Master Shen watches the old man lower himself onto the stool in stages.","zh":"參師父看著老人分幾次坐上凳子。"},{"who":"patient","en":"Ferryman Wu keeps both hands flat on his belly, the way you hold something warm.","zh":"吳老渡兩手平按腹上，像捧著什麼溫熱的東西。"},{"who":"boy","en":"The herb boy brings a second brazier without being asked.","zh":"藥童沒等吩咐，又搬了一個火盆來。"},{"who":"master","en":"\"He rows the first crossing before light. Ask him what happens before he reaches the boat.\"","zh":"「他天未亮就要撐頭一趟船。問他上船之前發生什麼事。」"},{"who":"patient","en":"\"Every morning, same time. I know the hour without a clock now.\"","zh":"「每天早上，都是那個時辰。如今不看更漏，我也知道。」"},{"who":"master","en":"\"A complaint that keeps an appointment is telling you something. Find out what.\"","zh":"「病能守時，必有所言。當究其所言為何。」"}],"remedy":{"ask":"cold_heat","look":"cold_heat","pulse":"cold_heat","dx":"excess_def","rx":"channel_organ","tech":"cold_heat"},"reward":{"cardEn":"The Fire at the Gate","cardZh":"命門火衰 · 溫補脾腎","cardTxt":"The Spleen does not transform food by itself — it is warmed from below by Kidney yang, the fire at the gate of life. Let that fire go low and two things follow from one cause: food passes through undigested, and water is no longer turned into vapour and moved, so it settles in the legs. Daybreak diarrhoea plus pitting oedema plus a cold aching low back is one pattern, not three complaints. Warm the yang and the water leaves on its own.","herbId":"aiye","herbEn":"Mugwort Leaf","herbZh":"艾葉","herbImg":"art/card-aiye.jpg","sprite":"art/sprite-renshen-jump.webp","herbTxt":"Bitter, acrid and warm, entering Liver, Spleen and Kidney. It warms the channels and disperses cold in the lower abdomen — and, dried and rolled, it is the moxa itself. In this case the herb and the technique are the same plant, which is worth noticing once and remembering always."},"endings":{"three":["Ten days on, Ferryman Wu sleeps to the sixth watch. \"I made the first crossing without stopping,\" he says. \"Twice this week.\"<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"You let the hour tell you the organ. The stool alone would have sent you to the Spleen and you would have warmed the middle and left the fire under it cold.\"","十日後，吳老渡能睡到六更。「頭一趟船我沒下船歇著，」他說，「這一旬有兩回。」<br><b>參師父：</b>「你由時辰而定其臟。若只憑便瀉，必歸之於脾，溫其中而遺其下之火。」"],"two":["The dawn waking is later, though not gone, and the ankles still hold a mark.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"Half the reasoning held. Go back to the swelling — you never asked it why it was there.\"","黎明而醒者稍遲，然未盡除，踝上按之猶留痕。<br><b>參師父：</b>「所推者得其半。回頭看那水腫——你不曾問它因何而在。」"],"one":["Nothing has changed, and he is apologetic about it, which is worse.<br><b>Master Shen:</b> \"He gave you the hour in his first sentence. Begin again there.\"","一如其舊，而他反來致歉，尤令人不安。<br><b>參師父：</b>「他頭一句話已把時辰給了你。從那裡重來。」"],"titles":["Ferryman Wu Sleeps Past Dawn","Ferryman Wu Is a Little Better","Ferryman Wu Rows Before Light"]},"script":[{"w":"master","en":"Cold weather brings us the old and the empty. Warm your hands before you touch him.","cn":"天寒，來的多是年老體虛之人。診他之前，先暖手。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Doctor. I pole the ferry at Stone Crossing. Thirty-one years.","cn":"大夫。我在石渡口撐船，三十一年了。"},{"w":"patient","en":"Something wakes me every morning before the cock. I have to run for the bushes, and after that I am wrung out for the whole day.","cn":"每天雞未啼，就給憋醒，非往草叢裡跑不可。跑完一整天沒力氣。"},{"w":"patient","en":"And my legs have gone heavy. My wife says I leave a dent in them when I take off my leggings.","cn":"腿也重了。內人說我脫綁腿的時候，腿上會留個坑。"},{"w":"master","en":"An hour, a stool, and a dent. Three facts, and they are not three illnesses. Ask him properly.","cn":"一個時辰、一種大便、一個凹痕。三事而非三病。好好問診。"}],"qa":[{"q":"What hour does it wake you — exactly?","cq":"確在何時而醒？","good":1,"a":"Fifth watch. Before first light, every day, near enough that I could set the ferry bell by it.","ca":"五更。天未亮，日日如是，準得可以照它敲渡口的鐘。","clue":{"en":"Diarrhoea at the fifth watch, before dawn","zh":"五更泄瀉，黎明而作"},"note":"Daybreak diarrhoea — <i>cock-crow diarrhoea</i> in the English exam wording — is the signature symptom of Spleen and Kidney yang deficiency. The fifth watch is when yin is exhausted and yang should be rising; a patient whose yang cannot rise loses the stool at exactly that hour. 五更泄瀉，英文考題作 daybreak / cock-crow diarrhea，為脾腎陽虛之標誌症。五更者，陰盡陽生之時；陽不能生，則瀉在此時。"},{"q":"What does the stool look like, and does it smell?","cq":"便下何狀？有無臭穢？","good":1,"a":"Loose, and I can pick out yesterday's millet in it. No smell to speak of.","ca":"溏薄，昨日的小米粒都認得出來。也沒什麼氣味。","clue":{"en":"Undigested food in loose stool, no foul odour","zh":"完穀不化，無臭穢"},"note":"Two findings, both pointing the same way. Undigested food means the Spleen is not transforming. The <i>absence</i> of a foul smell means there is no heat — heat rots and stinks, cold does not. Damp-heat diarrhoea is urgent, burning and foul; this is neither. 二證同歸。完穀不化者，脾失運化。無臭穢者，其中無熱——熱則腐而臭，寒則不然。濕熱之瀉，急迫、灼肛而穢臭，本案皆無。"},{"q":"Does anything ease the belly pain?","cq":"腹痛何以得緩？","good":1,"a":"A warm hand on it. Or sitting where the sun hits the deck.","ca":"用熱手按著就好些。或者坐在船板上曬得到太陽的地方。","clue":{"en":"Pain relieved by warmth and by pressure","zh":"腹痛喜溫喜按"},"note":"Relieved by warmth means cold; relieved by pressure means deficiency. Together — <i>likes warmth, likes pressure</i> — they read as empty cold. A full cold pattern would still like warmth but would refuse the hand. 得溫則減者寒，得按則減者虛。喜溫喜按，合而言之為虛寒。實寒者亦喜溫，然拒按。"},{"q":"Let me press your shin. Does the mark stay?","cq":"按其脛前，凹陷能復否？","good":1,"a":"It stays. My wife counts to ten before it fills back in.","ca":"不復。內人數到十，才慢慢平回去。","clue":{"en":"Pitting oedema of the legs","zh":"下肢凹陷性水腫"},"note":"Pitting oedema in a cold, weak patient is <i>yin water</i> — the yang cannot vaporise and move fluid, so it settles in the lowest place. Yang water is the opposite picture: sudden, starting at the face and eyelids, usually with an exterior pathogen. 虛寒之人而見凹陷性水腫，屬陰水——陽不化氣行水，水趨於下而停。陽水則反是：起病急，先見頭面眼瞼，多兼表邪。"},{"q":"And your water at night?","cq":"夜間小便如何？","good":1,"a":"Up three or four times. Clear as river water, and a lot of it.","ca":"夜起三四次。清如江水，且量多。","clue":{"en":"Frequent clear copious urination at night","zh":"夜尿頻，小便清長"},"note":"Clear and copious is cold; the Kidney is not holding or warming. Note that this sits beside oedema without contradiction — the Kidney yang can fail to transform fluid into vapour (so it pools in the legs) while also failing to contain it below (so it pours out at night). 小便清長屬寒，腎不溫不固。此與水腫並見而不相悖：腎陽不能化氣，故水停於下；不能固攝，故夜溺頻多。"},{"q":"How are your low back and knees?","cq":"腰膝如何？","good":1,"a":"Cold and sore. Like wet cloth wrapped round the bone, all winter.","ca":"又冷又痠。像濕布裹在骨頭上，整個冬天都這樣。","clue":{"en":"Cold aching low back and knees","zh":"腰膝冷痛"},"note":"The low back is the residence of the Kidney; cold there, with aching rather than sharp pain, is Kidney yang deficiency rather than a channel obstruction. This is the finding that lifts the case out of the Spleen alone. 腰為腎之府。冷而痠者，腎陽虛也，非經絡痹阻。有此一證，本案乃不止於脾。"},{"q":"Is your mouth bitter in the morning?","cq":"晨起口苦否？","good":0,"a":"Bitter? No. It tastes of nothing at all. Water tastes of nothing.","ca":"苦？不苦。什麼味也沒有。喝水也沒味。","clue":{"en":"No bitter taste; food and water taste of nothing","zh":"口不苦，飲食無味"},"note":"Not a wasted question — a negative can be evidence. A bitter mouth would have pulled you toward Liver or Gallbladder heat, and there is none. <i>Tasting nothing</i> is its own finding: the Spleen opens into the mouth, and a Spleen too weak to transform leaves food without savour. 問之非徒然——陰性所見亦為據。口苦者當責之肝膽有熱，本案無之。而「飲食無味」自為一證：脾開竅於口，脾虛不運，則食不知味。"}],"look":[{"t":"Pale and swollen, tooth-marked, with a white slippery coat","c":"舌淡胖有齒痕、苔白滑","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Pale swollen tooth-marked tongue, white slippery coat","zh":"舌淡胖有齒痕、苔白滑"},"note":"Correct, and read it as three separate statements. <b>Pale</b>: not enough yang and blood to bring colour up. <b>Swollen with tooth-marks</b>: fluid the Spleen has failed to move, pressing the tongue against the teeth. <b>White and slippery</b>: cold and wet, with no heat anywhere. 是，當作三句讀之。<b>淡</b>：陽血不足，不能上榮。<b>胖有齒痕</b>：脾不運濕，舌體脹而印於齒。<b>苔白而滑</b>：寒濕，通身無熱。"},{"t":"Red body with scant coating","c":"舌紅少苔","ok":0,"note":"That is yin deficiency — chapter thirteen. Everything about this man is cold and wet; a red tongue with no coat is hot and dry. The two are opposite halves of the same axis and the tongue is where the axis is easiest to read. 此陰虛之舌，第十三章是也。本案通身寒濕，而紅舌少苔者燥熱。二者一軸之兩端，而舌為最易辨處。"},{"t":"Greasy yellow coating","c":"苔黃膩","ok":0,"note":"Damp-heat. The damp is right and the heat is not. Ask what the yellow would have to mean here: heat in a man with clear urine, painless odourless stool and a slow pulse. 濕熱之苔。濕是而熱非。試問黃苔於此何解：小便清、便無臭、脈遲，而言有熱乎？"},{"t":"Pale with a thin white coat, not swollen","c":"舌淡苔薄白，體不胖","ok":0,"note":"Close, and this is the tongue of plain qi deficiency. What is missing is the water. Swelling and tooth-marks are what tell you fluid has stopped moving — without them you would not know to look at the legs. 近之，然此為單純氣虛之舌。所缺者水也。胖與齒痕，正告水濕已停；無此，則不知當察其下肢。"}],"pulse":[{"t":"Deep, slow and weak 沉遲無力","ok":1,"clue":{"en":"Deep slow weak pulse","zh":"脈沉遲無力"},"note":"Correct, and each of the three says something. <b>Deep</b>: the disease is interior, not on the surface. <b>Slow</b>: cold. <b>Weak</b>: deficiency. Deep-slow-weak together is the pulse of yang deficiency, and if you can only remember one, remember that <i>slow</i> is the one that says cold. 是，三者各有所主。<b>沉</b>：病在裡不在表。<b>遲</b>：寒。<b>無力</b>：虛。三者合為陽虛之脈。若只記一字，記「遲」——遲者主寒。"},{"t":"Thready and rapid 細數","ok":0,"note":"Yin deficiency with empty heat. Rapid is the problem: this man is cold from his tongue to his ankles. 陰虛有熱之脈。其病在「數」：本案自舌至踝，無一不寒。"},{"t":"Wiry 弦","ok":0,"note":"Constraint, and there is none here. Nothing is stuck — things are simply not being made or moved for want of warmth. 主鬱，本案無鬱。非有所滯，乃無火以化以行耳。"},{"t":"Slippery and forceful 滑而有力","ok":0,"note":"Phlegm or food with strength behind it. Force is the word to argue with — a pulse with force means there is a pathogen to push against, and here there is only shortage. 主痰主食，而其勢盛。當議者在「有力」：有力則有邪可爭，本案惟虛而已。"}],"dx":[{"ask":"Step 1 — the diarrhoea keeps an appointment. What does the hour tell you?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第一步：其瀉守時。時辰所告者何？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Daybreak is when yang should rise; his does not","c":"黎明陽當生而不生","ok":1,"note":"Correct. The fifth watch is the hinge of the day — yin at its last, yang not yet risen. A patient with enough yang crosses that hinge without noticing it. A patient whose fire at the gate of life has gone low cannot hold the bowel through the coldest, darkest, most yin hour there is, and loses it there every single day. The hour is not a detail; it is the diagnosis. 是。五更者，一日之樞：陰極而陽未升。陽足者過此樞而不覺。命門火衰者，當此至陰至寒之時，不能固其大腸，日日失之於此。時辰非細節，即診斷也。"},{"t":"The hour is incidental — only the stool matters","c":"時辰無關，惟大便可憑","ok":0,"note":"Then you have thrown away the single most examinable feature of this pattern. Loose stool has a dozen causes; loose stool <i>at daybreak, every day</i> has essentially one. When a symptom keeps time, the time is data. 若然，則棄本證最要之考點。便溏之因十數，而「日日黎明而瀉」者，其因幾一。症能守時，時即為據。"},{"t":"Dawn diarrhoea means damp-heat in the Intestines","c":"晨瀉為腸中濕熱","ok":0,"note":"Damp-heat diarrhoea is urgent and foul, burns on the way out, and comes with a bitter mouth, scanty dark urine, a greasy yellow coat and a rapid pulse. He has the opposite of all five. 濕熱之瀉：急迫穢臭、肛門灼熱，兼口苦、尿短赤、苔黃膩、脈數。此五者，本案皆反。"},{"t":"It is food stagnation from the evening meal","c":"晚食停滯所致","ok":0,"note":"Food stagnation is sour-smelling, comes with belching and a distended belly that <i>refuses</i> pressure, and it does not repeat at the same hour for a whole winter. His belly welcomes a warm hand. 食滯者噯腐吞酸、脘腹脹而拒按，且不至於一冬皆同時而作。本案腹則喜溫喜按。"}]},{"ask":"Step 2 — two organs are cold. Which one is the root, and which followed?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第二步：二臟俱寒。孰為其本，孰為其從？</small>","opts":[{"t":"Kidney is the root; the Spleen went cold after it","c":"腎為本，脾繼之而寒","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and the reason is physiological rather than a rule to memorise: the Spleen does not generate its own heat. Transformation in the middle burner is warmed from below by Kidney yang — the fire under the pot. Let that fire drop and the pot stops cooking, however good the pot is. His cold aching low back, his clear night urine and the hour of the diarrhoea all name the lower organ. 是，其理在生理而不在條文：脾不自生其熱。中焦運化，賴腎陽自下溫之，猶釜底之火。火衰則釜不熟物，釜雖良無益。腰膝冷痛、夜尿清長、瀉在五更——三者皆指其下。"},{"t":"Spleen is the root; the Kidney was drained later","c":"脾為本，久而累腎","ok":0,"note":"This chain is real and it does happen — chronic Spleen deficiency can exhaust the Kidney over years. But read the evidence in front of you: the timing, the back, the night urine and the oedema are all Kidney findings, and they are the loud ones. Direction matters because it decides which organ you warm first. 此傳變誠有之，久瀉傷脾，積年及腎。然當據所見：時辰、腰膝、夜尿、水腫，皆腎之候，且其證為著。定其向者，所以定先溫何臟也。"},{"t":"Both equally — there is no root","c":"二臟並重，無所謂本","ok":0,"note":"A comfortable answer that costs you the treatment. If there is no root there is no order of operations, and you will warm the middle, get three good days, and watch it come back. 此答安穩，而失其治。無本則無先後，將但溫其中，得三日之效，而後復如故。"},{"t":"The Large Intestine, since that is where the stool is","c":"病在大腸，以便所出故","ok":0,"note":"Where a symptom appears is not where it comes from. The Large Intestine here is downstream of both failures — it is the window, not the room. 症之所見，非病之所在。大腸於此在二虛之下流，乃其牖，非其室也。"}]},{"ask":"Step 3 — one yang has failed, yet you see two problems: undigested stool and standing water. Why?<br><small class=\"zh\" style=\"color:var(--ink-soft)\">第三步：陽虛惟一，而所見有二——完穀不化與水停為腫。何也？</small>","opts":[{"t":"One failure, two products — yang neither cooks food nor moves water","c":"一虛而二果：陽不腐熟，亦不化氣行水","ok":1,"note":"Correct, and this is the sentence the whole chapter exists for. Yang has two jobs here. It ripens and separates what you eat — without it, food passes through recognisable. And it turns fluid into vapour so the body can move it — without it, fluid stays liquid and sinks to the lowest place it can reach, which is the ankles of a man who stands on a boat all day. Two symptoms, two functions, one deficiency. Treat the deficiency and both go. 是，本章所為設者，正此一語。陽於此有二職：腐熟水穀而分清濁，失之則完穀不化；化氣行水而使之得行，失之則水停而趨下，聚於終日立於船上者之踝。二症、二職、一虛。治其虛，則二者俱去。"},{"t":"Two separate diseases in one unlucky man","c":"一人而二病相值","ok":0,"note":"Then you would write two prescriptions and fight yourself. The discipline of pattern differentiation is exactly this: find the one mechanism that explains every finding before you agree to call it two illnesses. 若然，則出二方而自相牴牾。辨證之功正在於此：必先求一機以貫諸證，而後乃許其為二病。"},{"t":"The oedema is a Lung problem — wind water","c":"水腫責之於肺，風水是也","ok":0,"note":"Wind water starts at the face and eyelids, comes on in days, and travels with an exterior pathogen and a floating pulse. His began at the ankles, over a winter, with a deep slow pulse and no exterior sign at all. Yin water and yang water are a standard examination pair — face-first and sudden versus feet-first and slow. 風水者先腫頭面眼瞼，起於數日，兼表邪而脈浮。本案起於足踝，歷一冬，脈沉遲而無表證。陰水陽水為考試必辨之對：一則面先而暴，一則足先而漸。"},{"t":"The oedema is damp-heat pooling below","c":"水腫為濕熱下注","ok":0,"note":"Damp-heat below brings burning urination, dark scanty urine, a greasy yellow coat and often itching or discharge. He passes clear water four times a night. 濕熱下注者小便灼熱短赤、苔黃膩，多兼癢或帶下。本案夜溺四次而清長。"}]}],"rx":[{"id":"KI7","t":"F&#249;li&#363; KI7 復溜","ok":1,"note":"The River point of the Kidney channel and the point that does this whole case at once — it warms Kidney yang, moves standing water, and stops chronic diarrhoea. Choosing it over Taixi KI3 is deliberate: KI3 restores whatever the Kidney is short of, while KI7 is the one that specifically moves water. 腎經經穴，一穴而該全案：溫腎陽、行停水、止久瀉。捨太谿而取此者有意：太谿補其所虧，而復溜專主行水。"},{"id":"ST36","t":"Z&#250;s&#257;nl&#464; ST36 足三里","ok":1,"note":"The Sea point of the Stomach and the great tonifying point of the middle. Warmed with moxa it rebuilds the transforming function that is letting food pass through whole. The Kidney is the root here, but a root without a middle burner to feed still leaves the man weak. 胃之合穴，補中之要穴。加灸則復其運化，止其完穀不化。腎雖為本，然無中焦以資之，其人終虛。"},{"id":"SP6","t":"S&#257;ny&#299;nji&#257;o SP6 三陰交","ok":1,"note":"Where the Spleen, Liver and Kidney channels meet — one needle on two of the organs at fault. It strengthens the Spleen, supports the Kidney and promotes the movement of water, which is precisely the three-part job this case asks for. 足三陰交會之處，一針而及二病之臟。健脾、益腎、利水，正合本案三事。"},{"id":"SP9","t":"Y&#299;nl&#237;ngqu&#225;n SP9 陰陵泉","ok":0,"note":"The point for draining damp, and draining is the objection. This water is standing because nothing is warm enough to move it — open a channel out of an already empty man and you take fluid he needs while the cause sits untouched. Drain damp when there is damp <i>and</i> strength; warm the yang when there is neither. 利濕之要穴，而所議在「利」。本案水停，以無陽以行之故。虛極而導其出，則奪其所賴，而其因如故。濕實而正未虛者利之；陽虛者溫之。"},{"id":"LU5","t":"Ch&#464;z&#233; LU5 尺澤","ok":0,"note":"The Lung's Sea point, used for oedema when the Lung is failing to regulate the water passages from above — the wind-water picture. That is not this. This water fails from below. 肺之合穴，治水腫者，為肺失通調水道於上，即風水之屬。本案不然，其失自下而起。"},{"id":"LR3","t":"T&#224;ich&#333;ng LR3 太衝","ok":0,"note":"Source point of the Liver, for constraint and for Liver deficiency. There is no constraint here — no wandering pain, no wiry pulse, no emotional trigger, no sighing. A good point in the wrong chapter. 肝之原穴，主鬱及肝虛。本案無鬱：痛不走竄、脈不弦、不因情志、不善太息。穴良而非其章。"}],"tech":[{"t":"Reinforcing method, with generous moxa","c":"補法，重灸","ok":1,"note":"<b>Correct, and here the moxa is not an addition — it is the treatment.</b> Everything in this case is empty, so reinforce; everything is cold, so warm. Moxa is withheld for heat and for dryness, and this man has neither anywhere: pale wet tongue, clear urine, odourless stool, slow pulse. Note what you are holding in your hand while you do it — mugwort, the herb this chapter gives you. 二者皆是，而灸非佐助，即其治也。通案皆虛，故補；通案皆寒，故溫。忌灸者為熱為燥，本案自舌至脈無一見之：舌淡潤、尿清、便不臭、脈遲。行灸之時，且看手中所持何物——艾也，即本章所授之藥。"},{"t":"Drain the water first, then warm the yang","c":"先利其水，後溫其陽","ok":0,"note":"The order is backwards, and this is the classic error with yin water. Draining first takes fluid from a man who is already empty, gives you two or three good days, and leaves the cold yang exactly where it was — so the water comes back, and he is weaker when it does. Warm the yang and the water moves itself. 其序倒置，陰水之常誤在此。先利則奪虛人之津，得二三日之效，而寒陽如故；水復停而其人益虛。溫其陽，則水自行。"},{"t":"Reducing method, to clear the standing water","c":"瀉法，以逐其停水","ok":0,"note":"Reducing needs something full to reduce. Read the pulse again: deep, slow and <i>weak</i>. Force is what tells you a pathogen is there to be pushed against, and there is none. 瀉者必有實可瀉。再察其脈：沉、遲而<b>無力</b>。有力者乃有邪可爭，本案無之。"},{"t":"Reinforcing method, but no moxa","c":"補法，不施灸","ok":0,"note":"Cautious in the wrong case. You withhold moxa for heat, for dryness, for a red peeled tongue, for a rapid pulse — the picture in chapter thirteen. Here the caution costs you most of the effect. 其慎失所。忌灸者，為熱、為燥、為舌紅而剝、為脈數——第十三章是也。於此而慎，則失其效之大半。"}]};
